{title: 440 - How Cheering Is the Christian's Hope}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #440 • EXORTATION • 8.8.4.9.6.9.6}
{lyricist: Anon}
{composer: S. Hibbard}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 440}
{meta: tune EXORTATION}
{meta: meter 8.8.4.9.6.9.6}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]How cheer [A]ing [D]is the Chris tian’s [G]hope,
[A7]While [D]toil [A]ing [D]herebelow!
[D/F#](It [G]bouys [D/F#]us [G]up)
[A7/E]It bouys [D]us [A]up while [Em]passing through
[D]This [F#m]wilderness [D]of woe,
[D]It buoys [Em]us [A]up while [A7]passing [D]through
[D]This [Bm]wilderness [G]of [A7]woe.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]It bouys [A]us [D]up [A/C#]while [D]this passing through
[D/F#]This wilderness of [G]woe,
[D]It bouys [F#m]us [D]up while passing through
[D]This [Bm]wilderness [G]of [A7]woe.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]It points [A]us [D]to a land of [G]rest,
[D/F#]Where saints [G]with [D/F#]Christ will [G]reign;
[D]Where [F#m]we [D]shall meet the loved of earth,
[D]And [Bm]never [G]part again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Fly, lingering [A/C#]moments, [D]fly, O, [G]fly,
[D/F#]Dear Savior, quickly [G]come!
[D]We [F#m]long [D]to see Thee as Thou art,
[D]And [Bm]reach [D]that [G]blissful [A7]home.
{end_of_verse}
